    The compiled run's generics: the first load takes the JDK's lock, tasks are generic, arms are dispatched at the template's parameters, and clause names are bound

    Climb batch 6.5, rung G (PLAN phase 2b; rows 417, 419, 420, 351, 426). The
    class loader's loadClass now runs under getClassLoadingLock(name), the lock
    the JDK's own loadClass takes and the override had dropped, so a generic
    arm's first load is safe on four threads; CodeGen.delegate makes a task class
    generic over its free static parameters, as forFnExpr does for a closure,
    which also closes row 420; OverloadSet.generateCall reads each generic arm of
    a template dispatcher at the dispatcher's own static parameters by position,
    which fixes the renamed-arm and ZZ32 dispatch defects (rows 493 and 494); and
    forTypecase and forTry bind a clause's name as a local, which is why the
    compiled cast[\T\] never matched (row 426). Answer 7's identity functions pass
    a typed binding through cast in their ZZ32 and RR64 branches.

    Folded at the gather: REPORT.md and record.md written from the worker's
    structured result, the skeptic's five corrections made (the dispatch guard
    stated as the code has it, with the class of arms it moves, row 499; row 351's
    reach in a do ... also arm and for a pattern-bound name; row 460's note; the
    home-3 grep and decision), rows 493 to 496 and the skeptic's 497 to 499, the
    home-2 pair XXXTaskArmLocalSlot for row 497 shown red on the fix, notes on
    rows 159, 322, 340 and 460, the items for Pavol in PLAN.md, present-tense
    library citations re-anchored by 8, and the batch record begun.

    historical: ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/runtimeSystem/InstantiatingClassloader.java, ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java, ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/OverloadSet.java, Library/FortressLibrary.fss (additiveIdentity and multiplicativeIdentity). The tests added or promoted in ProjectFortress/compiler_tests/ and library_tests/ are the revival's own.

